{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
  "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Xavier Becerra, Secretary of HHS)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Medicare fraction directs HHS to count patient days of patients who, for such days, were entitled to benefits under Part A of Medicare. The question here is which patients are entitled to Part A benefits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Empire Health Foundation)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent contends that the agency's approach to SSI benefits conflicts with its position here. That is not correct, as the agency explained in the 2010 regulation and as the Sixth Circuit explained in Metro Hospital."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Bond, before we get bogged down in this indecipherable language, what does -- what's the difference between \"entitled to\" and \"eligible for\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But, Mr. Bond, you are interpreting the word \"entitled\" to mean something different in the same sentence, different with respect to Medicare and SSI. So that's problem one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, how do you -- or do we give you any Chevron deference for this interpretation? Are you relying on that at all, or are you taking the position that this is what the statute plainly says even though, as Justice Kavanaugh pointed out, that's subject to a great deal of dispute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Xavier Becerra, Secretary of HHS)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOND: We do think we are entitled to Chevron deference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Bond, I have a question about the difference between SSI and Medicare Part A and the use of the word \"entitled.\" If I understand your argument, you said in response to Justice Kavanaugh that the distinction was that, for Medicare, eligibility or entitlement arises directly by operation of law, whereas, for SSI, it occurs after a determination, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Is that always true for Medicare Part A, however? I mean, I see why it's true for seniors, for people who are over 65. But it's my understanding that for people who are entitled to it based on disability, there did have to be a determination because somebody has to say that, in fact, you're disabled and you qualify."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But why is that different? It doesn't arise magically by operation of law if someone is disabled and it's unclear whether the disability qualifies, just in the same way that it doesn't arise magically by operation of law that someone's entitled to SSI. Both depend on a predicate determination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, if I think that you both have reasonable interpretations, what should we do with the Encino issue? Should we decide it? Do we have to decide it? Should it be just --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But wasn't it unclear what the commenters thought they were being asked to comment on? In other words, a commenter who said I approve of the status quo, it was unclear whether that was the real status quo or the status quo as mis-described by the agency?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federation of American Hospitals",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federation of American Hospitals, one of Respondent's own amici, said that the agency lacked statutory authority to do what Respondent is now urging."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, that's quite a job. I mean, do I understand this correctly? And the chances I understand it correctly are near zero, okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: To pick up on the Chief Justice's earlier question and Justice Gorsuch's question about the through line, it seems from a 30,000-foot level that the through line is the agency wanting to spend as little as possible on this program because entitlement spending, mandatory spending, is a huge part of the federal budget, and the agency, especially in 2003, '4, '5, the new prescription drug benefit had just come in, which was going to be a huge new expenditure for the government, and so the government, the administration at that time, was looking for places to restrain the growth or cut, in government speak, spending."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: One final question. Do you agree, though, that the agency's approach from the mid-'80s through those four courts of appeals was to lower payments beyond -- compared to what it would have otherwise been, and then its approach, starting in '03, '04, '05, similarly was to lower payments compared to what it otherwise would have been?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Yeah, but -- but --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: -- but that isn't what the statute says. The statute says \"entitled to benefits under Part A of Medicare.\" MR. HETTICH: Uh- huh."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, you -- you and Mr. Bond have both said a lot about what Congress intended, but do you really think that a majority of the Senate and a majority of the House thought through the particular question that faces us in this case and they all said, yes, your interpretation is the right interpretation, that's what we want? Do you seriously want to make that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Have we left out any other reason why yours is the better reason or the better reading, I'm sorry?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I ask how the \"for such days\" worked in practice in the first two decades? You would go -- someone would go through and say this patient on November 10 received Medicare benefits for that hospital stay. On November 11, they've received Medicare. On November 12, they did not. Is that -- it was done at that granular level, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3cd1733405b188e0515be120ce13532626827088b86f6d8a73518c41385c28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3cd1733405-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Just one question. Are there -- are inpatient services the only benefits under Part A? Because we've spent -- I think so much of your argument is premised on that being the only benefit and that that benefit would be exhausted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1312",
